          "linkId": "img-body",
          "text": "Ultra-widefield or fundus photographs document the retina and can reveal diabetic retinopathy, macular degeneration, glaucoma suspects, moles, holes, and detachments. Screening images do not always replace a dilated exam, especially with flashes, floaters, high myopia, or diabetes. Vision and medical plans usually do not cover screening photos. The posted fee is due today unless the doctor orders photos as a medical procedure.",
